  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Wireless charging needs no metal plug between the pad and your phone. It passes energy through a magnetic field. Inside the pad, alternating current flows through a coil. That current makes the magnetic field rise and fall. A second coil inside your phone sits within that field. The changing magnetism induces a voltage in this coil. The phone turns that induced power into a form its battery can use. The coils work best when they are close and aligned. Distance and misalignment weaken the link and waste energy. So the cable disappears but a pair of coils still makes the connection.",
